<description>
Extend the 2x2 seed diagonally from each red corner, recoloring every stamped cell with the seed's non-red color.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background color.
- All foreground pixels form one full 2x2 seed block.
- The seed contains one non-red paint color and one or more red corner control pixels.

Rule
- Replace every red control pixel with the paint color.
- A red pixel in the top-left, top-right, bottom-left, or bottom-right corner selects the matching diagonal direction.
- For each selected direction, repeatedly stamp a filled 2x2 square of the paint color one row and one column at a time until the square is fully outside the grid.

Key insight
- The red pixels are not output colors; their corner positions encode the diagonal rays along which the 2x2 seed is copied.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "full 2x2 seed block containing red corner control pixels and one non-red paint color",
  "path": "from each red corner, diagonal ray in the matching corner direction",
  "trajectory": "copy a filled 2x2 square of the paint color one cell at a time along each ray, clipped at the grid boundary",
  "transform": "red seed pixels become the paint color; all painted cells use the seed's non-red color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 9x9 [observed], background black
  seed:
    shape: exactly 2x2, fully occupied (no bg cells)
    colors: exactly 1 paint color (any non-red, non-black) + 1-3 red corner pixels
    red_corners: 1-3 cells of the 2x2 are red; remaining cells are paint color
    position: at least 1 cell from every grid edge [observed]; min ray length >= 4
  output:
    background: black (same as input)
    content: for each red corner, a diagonal ray of 2x2 paint-color stamps
    ray_direction: red at TL -> up-left, TR -> up-right, BL -> down-left, BR -> down-right
    ray_stamping: starting at seed position, step +/-1 row and +/-1 col per stamp, until fully off-grid
    overlap: multiple rays may overlap; all painted cells use the same paint color
    seed_itself: painted with paint color (red replaced)
    ray_length: 4-7 stamps per ray [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct (constraints are simple enough for forward generation)
  steps:
    1. Create 9x9 black grid
    2. Pick paint_color from {1,3,4,5,6,7,8,9} (non-red, non-black)
    3. Pick seed top-left position (r0, c0) ensuring min ray length >= 4
       for every chosen red corner direction, i.e. the ray in that direction
       must take >= 4 steps before fully exiting the grid
    4. Choose 1-3 corners of the 2x2 to be red; fill remaining with paint_color
    5. Place seed on grid to form the input
    6. To build output, run the solver logic: for each red corner stamp 2x2
       paint along its diagonal until off-grid
```
</generation_spec>
